        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk2-manner-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Describe how an action is done",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "地 can introduce a manner or attitude before an action. 得 follows the action and describes its performance or resulting state. With an expressed object, repeat the verb before 得 or place the object before the verb as a topic; do not insert it between 得 and the description.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "她高兴地来了。",
                "pinyin": "tā gāoxìng de lái le 。",
                "meaning": "She came happily.",
                "audio": "dcee88d7d557521666ef29b0cc23798d6156b28ccded0decd9ee820bb0d24efc"
              },
              {
                "text": "他说得很好。",
                "pinyin": "tā shuō de hěn hǎo 。",
                "meaning": "He speaks well.",
